  [-]add <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Add item to given list
  [-]analyse <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Perform timing analysis
  [-]assert <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Set limits on the analysis phase
  [-]config <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Configures the given option
  [-]clear: Clears the screen (Gui mode only)
  [-]echo "text": prints the text to the console
  [-]exit: Quits the shell (Standalone mode only)
  [-]help [command]: Displays help message for the given command
  [-]history: Displays the command history
  [-]load <xe file>: Loads the given xmos executable file
  [-]list <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Lists the given set of items
  [-]print <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Display path information
  [-]pwd: Displays the current working directory
  [-]remove <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Remove item from given list
  [-]set <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Set path information
  [-]source <file name>: Sources the given command file
  [-]status: Display current status
  [-]summary <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Display timing summaries
  [-]unset <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Unset item from given list
  [-]version: Displays the version information
  [-]add <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Add item to given list
      option: filter <ref>: Adds the given reference to the filter list (post analysis action)
      option: prohibited <ref>: Adds the given reference to the prohibited list (pre analysis action)
      option: required <ref>: Adds the given reference to the required list (post analysis action)
      option: branch <from ref> <to ref>: Adds the given from/to reference to the branches list
      option: endpoint <ref> <label>: Adds the given endpoint to the endpoints list
      option: label <ref> <label>: Adds the given label to the labels list
  [-]analyse <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Perform timing analysis
      option: path <from ref> <to ref>: Sets a path start and end points
      option: function <name>: Sets a path to trace a given function
  [-]assert <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Set limits on the analysis phase
      option: maxtime <ns> : Analysis fails at the given time limit
      option: maxcycles <num cycles> : Analysis fails at the given cycle limit
  [-]clear: Clears the screen (Gui mode only)
  [-]config <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Configures the given option
      option: proc <node id> <core id>: All following analysis on given node and core (default: 0,0)
      option: freq <core frequency>: Sets the core frequency (default: 400)
      option: threads <num threads>: Sets number of threads currently executing (default: 8)
      option: srcpaths <paths>: Sets the (semicolon separated) source search path
  [-]echo "text": prints the text to the console
  [-]exit: Quits the shell (Standalone mode only)
  [-]help [command]: Displays help message for the given command
  [-]history: Displays the command history
  [-]list <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Lists the given set of items
      option: filters: Lists the reference in the filter list
      option: prohibited: Lists the reference in the excluded list
      option: required: Lists the reference in the excluded list
      option: branches: Lists the branches
      option: labels: Lists the labels
      option: endpoints: Lists the endpoints
      option: alllabels: Lists all the possible locations for labels
      option: allendpoints: Lists all the possible locations for endpoints
      option: unknowns : Displays a list of the unknowns within the current analysis
      option: functions: Lists the functions in the loaded application
      option: sources: Lists the source files
      option: times: Lists the instructions which have had their times set
      option: queries: Lists the current queries
  [-]load <xe file>: Loads the given xmos executable file
  [-]print <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Display path information
      option: asm <path/block id>: Display annotated assembly for given path id
      option: src <path/block id>: Display annotated source file(s) for given path id
      option: mix <path/block id>: Display annotated source file(s) + assembly instructions for the given path id
      option: trace <path/block id>: Display instruction trace for the given path/block
  [-]pwd: Displays the current working directory
  [-]remove <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Remove item from given list
      option: filter <ref>: Removes the given reference from the filter list (supports regular expressions)
      option: prohibited <ref>: Removes the given reference from the prohibited list (supports regular expressions)
      option: required <ref>: Removes the given reference from the required list (post analysis action)
      option: branch <from ref>: Removes the given from reference from the branches list
      option: endpoint [label]+: Removes the given endpoints from the endpoints list (supports regular expressions)
      option: label [label]+: Removes the given labels from the labels list (supports regular expressions)
  [-]set <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Set path information
      option: loop <path> <scope> <iterations>: Sets the number of iterations for the given path
          scope: relative/r: Iteration number propagates to the enclosing path (Default)
          scope: absolute/a: Absolute number of iterations
      option: time <ref> <mode> <value>: Sets the time taken for the instruction at the given pc
          mode: ns:     Sets the time this instruction takes in ns
          mode: cycles: Sets the time this instruction takes in thread cycles
  [-]source <file name>: Sources the given command file
  [-]status: Display current status
  [-]summary <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Display timing summaries
      option: simple: Show simple paths summary
      option: complete: Show timing of complete path(s)
      option: complete_loops: Show timing of complete path(s) + loops
      option: complete_blocks: Show timing of complete path(s) + loops + blocks
      option: complete_instructions: Show timing of complete path(s) + loops + blocks + instructions
      option: unresolved: Show timing of unresolved path(s)
      option: unresolved_loops: Show timing of complete path(s) + loops
      option: unresolved_blocks: Show timing of complete path(s) + loops + blocks
      option: unresolved_instructions: Show timing of complete path(s) + loops + blocks + instructions
      option: functions: Show path(s) + functions
      option: sources: Show path(s) + sources
      option: info <path/block id>: Show information for given path/block
  [-]unset <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Unset item from given list
      option: time <pc>: Clears the time set for the given instructions (supports regular expressions)
